If you can keep monster level low (as one does on the racket) the odds of
the item being given are low. Then rnd_offensive_item() makes all kinds of
calculations based on MONSTR. The practical upshot of it is you're not
going to see wands other than striking on monsters on a racket run, and
relatively few of those.

>>[...] If you can't deal with
>>floating eyes (/make invisible, !blindness, /teleportation,...) going
>>past dlvl4 is a big no no.
>Why that? And, WRT floating eyes, is dlvl 4 different in the mines
>than in the main branch?

Floating eyes have a MONSTR of 3, so will only likely turn up at depth 5
with XL 1. It's easy to get stuck behind one on a main branch level, and
since they are worth 17 experience, you're going to be cutting it pretty
fine on hitting the Mine Town at XL 1 if you kill one.

Mines levels do not get generated with floating eyes normally, and
"Monster creation in this branch is biased towards lawful monsters" which,
well, I forget what that means specifically, but eyes don't as a rule turn
up in the Mines - given the dark levels, they'd be YASD-city otherwise.

